            <ArticleTitle>Coronary angioplasty of branch vessels associated with an extreme angle take-off.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>356-9</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Stenoses in branch vessels which originate at acute angle to the main vessel represent a technically challenging anatomy for the performance of balloon angioplasty [PTCA]. We report a novel technique utilizing a distally placed perfusion balloon that facilitated guidewire placement and subsequent balloon angioplasty of a branch vessel stenosis.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
